\ SAVE(x squared + a*x + b*drop[i-1] + c*drop[i-3] +
\ d*drop[i-7] + the selected stone).
To grind a visible drop:
  Choose the visible grinding recipe.
  Put the visible work's value into a result wide quantity.
  Multiply the visible work's value by the result wide quantity.
  Put the visible work's value into a weighted wide quantity.
  Multiply the weighted wide quantity by the visible work's value factor.
  Add the weighted wide quantity to the result wide quantity.
  Put the previous drops' first previous into the weighted wide quantity.
  Multiply the weighted wide quantity by the visible work's first previous factor.
  Add the weighted wide quantity to the result wide quantity.
  Put the previous drops' third previous into the weighted wide quantity.
  Multiply the weighted wide quantity by the visible work's third previous factor.
  Add the weighted wide quantity to the result wide quantity.
  Put the previous drops' seventh previous into the weighted wide quantity.
  Multiply the weighted wide quantity by the visible work's seventh previous factor.
  Add the weighted wide quantity to the result wide quantity.
  Add the visible work's grinding stone to the result wide quantity.
  Keep the result wide quantity for the sauce.
  Put the result wide quantity into the visible work's value.

\ Insert a finished drop in front of the last seven previous values.
\ Shift from oldest to newest so nothing is overwritten too early.
To remember the new visible drop:
  Put the previous drops' sixth previous into the previous drops' seventh previous.
  Put the previous drops' fifth previous into the previous drops' sixth previous.
  Put the previous drops' fourth previous into the previous drops' fifth previous.
  Put the previous drops' third previous into the previous drops' fourth previous.
  Put the previous drops' second previous into the previous drops' third previous.
  Put the previous drops' first previous into the previous drops' second previous.
  Put the visible work's value into the previous drops' first previous.

\ All eleven grinding steps are completed before updating history.
To make a visible drop given a number:
  Put the number into the visible work's index.
  Reach the stones for the number.
  Make the visible dough.
  Put 1 into the visible work's grinding step.
  Loop.
    If the visible work's grinding step is greater than 11, break.
    Grind the visible drop.
    Add 1 to the visible work's grinding step.
  Repeat.
  Put the visible work's value into the last visible drop.
  Remember the new visible drop.

\ The sauce input must already contain the five exact counters.
\ The requested last drop must be between 1 and 46 inclusive.
To make visible drops through a number:
  Make all seven hidden drops.
  Prepare the previous drops.
  Put 1 into a visible position number.
  Loop.
    If the visible position number is greater than the number, break.
    If the visible position number is greater than 46, break.
    Make a visible drop given the visible position number.
    Add 1 to the visible position number.
  Repeat.
